      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd `min_tokens` support to the Responses API request path and forward it to `SamplingParams`. Fixes #64009.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `/v1/responses` accepts the vLLM-specific `min_tokens` request parameter.\n- The value reaches engine sampling with the same default (`0`) used by the chat and completions protocols.\n- A serving-path regression covers request parsing and validation, while a focused unit test covers the protocol-to-sampling mapping.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Baseline focused regression on `5314c582817faa57bc2fb0acdf05fdb6bbe97c3c`: failed because `sampling_params.min_tokens` remained `0` instead of the requested value. Current main `90309f6b742cdb1d6305778b81063918cf61be81` was separately inspected and still omits the field and forwarding.\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_sampling_params.py -q`: **11 passed**.\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest --collect-only -q tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_simple.py::test_min_tokens_validation`: **1 test collected**.\n- `.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files vllm/entrypoints/openai/responses/protocol.py tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_sampling_params.py tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_simple.py`: **passed**, including Ruff, mypy, CI test tethering, SPDX, and config validation.\n- `git diff --check`: **passed**.\n\nThe serving-path test was also started locally, but the test server could not initialize because this CPU environment lacks the compiled `vllm._C_AVX2` / `torch.ops._C.init_cpu_memory_env` operation. The test is selected by the existing Responses API integration CI step.\n\nModel evaluation is not applicable because this only exposes and forwards an existing sampling parameter; it does not change model implementation, accuracy, or sampling semantics.\n\n## Details\n\nThe Responses request schema omitted `min_tokens`, so the field never reached `SamplingParams.from_optional` and the engine used its default of `0`. The patch adds the field inside the existing rendered Responses API extra-parameters snippet and forwards it through the existing sampling conversion.\n\nThe serving regression submits `min_tokens=2` with `max_output_tokens=1` through `RemoteOpenAIServer` and requires the engine's exact user-facing validation error. Without forwarding, that request is accepted because the engine sees `min_tokens=0`.\n\nThis does not duplicate an existing fix. Immediately before implementation and publication, searches across open and closed PRs by issue number, `ResponsesRequest min_tokens`, and `responses API min_tokens` found no PR implementing this issue. The older merged sampling-parameter PR #32609 explicitly left `min_tokens` out.\n\nAI assistance was used to investigate, implement, test, and independently review this change. I reviewed every changed line and reran the checks above on the exact submitted head.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
