    {
      "body": "Independent real-server check of the exact `protocol.py` versions from `90309f6b` and `2ddbc4a`, using published Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct weights on B300 / Torch 2.14.0+cu130:\n\n- `min_tokens=2, max_output_tokens=1`: HTTP 200 before, HTTP 400 with the expected validation error after.\n- `min_tokens=-1`: HTTP 200 before, HTTP 400 after.\n- Default sampling and `min_tokens=max_output_tokens=1` both remain valid; the latter returns one output token.\n\nThe same four checks gave **2 passed / 2 failed before, 4 passed after**, with no skips or fixture errors. Both original failures were `DID NOT RAISE BadRequestError`.\n\nThis was an AI-assisted, source-verified module overlay on the existing `5d35ce39` Python / `0f6b2619` native environment, in eager mode. It corroborates forwarding and HTTP validation, not the full PR build, Qwen3-8B CI, PD freeze diagnosis, accuracy or performance. Earlier startup failures were retained separately and not counted as bug reproductions.",
